CORSY scans a target website to find dangerous CORS configurations such as: Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * with credentials
                                                                            Reflected origins (any domain you send is allowed)
                                                                            Overly permissive subdomain trust
                                                                            Insecure wildcard patterns


These issues can allow data theft, account takeover, or token leakage via malicious websites.


Installation :
1.git clone https://github.com/s0md3v/Corsy.git
cd Corsy
python3 -m venv sai
source sai/bin/activate                                                  
pip3 install -r requirements.txt
deactivate


Usage : python3 corsy.py -u https://example.com




2.git clone https://github.com/RUB-NDS/CORStest.git 
cd CORStest
python3 corstest.py file.txt
